{"id": "lesson_d892d844cf60", "claim": "Do small, directly-related follow-up tasks in the same session, never defer them as a vague 'follow-up'. Procrastination leads to forgetting and stale/overdue debt.", "conditions": ["defer", "followup", "immediate", "procrastination"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T09:21:23.688000"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T09:21:23.747259", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "User-stated 2026-06-22. Context is freshest the moment the related need surfaces; deferred 'I'll flag it later' items are exactly what gets forgotten.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "d892d844cf60"}
{"id": "lesson_0afc8c5f2778", "claim": "Before acting on a repo, verify you are not on a stale branch: fetch and compare the local HEAD tree to origin (tree-twin, not ahead/behind counts), and adopt upstream structural migrations before writing.", "conditions": ["branch", "fetch", "migration", "origin", "outdated", "stale", "tree-twin"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T09:21:23.812031"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T09:21:23.850084", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22: I committed into the dead '.agents/memory' dir while origin/main had already migrated the memory system to '.agent/'. I was outdated and did not know it because I never checked origin before writing.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "0afc8c5f2778"}
