{"id": "lesson_d0d49b68ab24", "claim": "Complete gbrain source archival/removal in the SAME pass you decide it — never leave 'pending removal'. Old-path duplicate sources (from repo moves) left un-archived resurface as sync_freshness/multi_source_drift warnings every session. Prefer 'gbrain sources archive' (reversible) + export the def to ~/repo-backups first; the orama guard scripts/gbrain/gbrain-selfheal.sh acks failures, refreshes live sources, and reports orphans automatically. Autopilot is launchd KeepAlive: stop with 'launchctl unload -w', a kill won't stick.", "conditions": ["archive", "autopilot", "gbrain", "launchd", "pending", "removal", "selfheal", "source", "stale"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T10:28:21.564630"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T10:28:21.607031", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22: gbrain sync kept needing manual re-fixing. Root causes: (1) autopilot --repo . jammed on 204 unacked parse failures, silently staling sources; (2) old-path duplicate sources from the iCloud-escape/~code moves were quarantined 06-18 but left 'pending removal', recurring as stale alarms. Built orama self-heal + archived the orphans to close the loop.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "d0d49b68ab24"}
{"id": "lesson_5b891b07e193", "claim": "Recurring miss: I keep writing literal workstation paths (workspace-root shorthand path, a synced workspace tree) into TRACKED docs, then only fix them after the no-workstation-paths hook / LINT-006 blocks me. Write paths abstractly the FIRST time: $OPENCLAW_ROOT / $REPO_ROOT / repo-relative (../../<repo>/) / username-containing placeholders. Check the path-hygiene rule BEFORE writing a doc, not after the block.", "conditions": ["docs", "hook", "lint-006", "openclaw-tree", "portable", "repo-relative", "workstation-path"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T10:48:56.625356"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T10:48:56.665127", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22: blocked twice in one turn writing the gbrain self-heal journey doc; also re-leaked 2026-06-12 (per CIDF LINT-006 note). The block is the LATE backstop; the habit is to think portable-paths up front. Deeper meta: check the established guard/convention before producing the artifact.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "5b891b07e193"}
{"id": "lesson_legacy_ad245568f6b1", "claim": "When merging branches that both append to .agent memory (lessons.jsonl, episodic/AGENT_LEARNINGS.jsonl), resolve conflicts by UNION — keep both sides, dedup by lesson 'id' (jsonl) or by line (episodic) — then RE-RENDER LESSONS.md from lessons.jsonl via render_lessons.py (never hand-merge the rendered file, AGENTS.md Rule 5). Sanitize any leaked workstation paths using relative paths or env vars (not username placeholders), or pre-commit repo_hygiene (LINT-006) blocks the merge commit. Use a throwaway git worktree to resolve without disturbing main's working tree.", "conditions": [], "evidence_ids": [], "status": "legacy", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T11:59:40.912062+00:00", "reviewer": "render_lessons_migration", "rationale": "Imported from pre-restructure LESSONS.md bullets below sentinel", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 5.0, "confidence": 0.7, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": null}
