{"id": "lesson_1bb7057c6ea8", "claim": "When a git pre-push hook runs from a deleted or removed worktree directory (getcwd fails), the hook exits non-zero with 'banned or unapproved attribution in commits to push' — even when NO actual banned pattern exists. The banned_attribution_lib.sh cannot resolve the repo root or patterns file, so it fails closed. The error message is misleading: the real cause is a dead working directory, not a real attribution violation. Fix: never delete a worktree before the git push completes; if a push fails with this message after a worktree cleanup, re-push from a live worktree or the canonical repo directory.", "conditions": ["attribution", "banned", "deleted", "getcwd", "hook", "misleading-error", "pre-push", "removed", "worktree"], "evidence_ids": ["2026-06-22T22:11:11.020066"], "status": "accepted", "accepted_at": "2026-06-22T22:11:11.112517", "reviewer": "learn.py", "rationale": "2026-06-22: PT #127 branch push blocked with 'banned or unapproved attribution' after the <local-temp> worktree was removed (git worktree remove --force) before the push command finished. The commits had Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com> which is explicitly allowed (anthropic.com in WELL_KNOWN_COAUTHOR_DOMAIN_SUFFIXES). Confirmed: re-pushing from a fresh worktree with the same commits (after squash) succeeded immediately.", "cluster_size": 1, "canonical_salience": 8.0, "confidence": 0.6, "support_count": 0, "contradiction_count": 0, "supersedes": null, "source_candidate": "1bb7057c6ea8"}
